1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,910
Action Receipt helps students turn a notice into actions they can check against the original.

2
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:09,880
This invented notice contains no personal student information.

3
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:16,550
The local text rules find three proposals and flag two passages for review.

4
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,275
Nothing starts approved.

5
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:22,310
The complete source stays available alongside the proposed actions.

6
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:28,830
Registration and the bus deposit keep separate deadlines and exact source quotations.

7
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:32,380
A quotation match still needs a person to check the meaning.

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,150
The rules missed the consent form.

9
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:39,950
The source review creates a separate action from that exact passage.

10
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:44,565
It is labeled as an addition, with no invented deadline or automatic approval.

11
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,885
The separate membership fee is waived.

12
00:00:49,885 --> 00:00:57,295
Recording it as not an obligation preserves the explanation without creating another payment task or
calendar event.

13
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:03,200
Action approval and date confirmation are separate checks.

14
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,780
Registration has a complete date.

15
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:11,360
Confirming that date allows an approved registration action to become an all day calendar marker.

16
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:14,930
The deposit has a timed cutoff.

17
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:22,680
Its date, five P M time, and explicit U T C minus ten offset must all be checked before it can enter the
calendar.

18
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,885
Accessible transport applies only if needed.

19
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:31,295
Next Friday stays unresolved.

20
00:01:31,295 --> 00:01:37,755
The undated consent form and conditional email can remain checklist tasks, without guessed calendar
dates.

21
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:43,505
After these review choices, the checklist contains four approved actions.

22
00:01:43,505 --> 00:01:48,370
Only the two actions with complete, confirmed dates qualify for the calendar.

23
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:52,465
The preview shows the exact checklist text.

24
00:01:52,465 --> 00:01:57,895
Approved actions keep supporting quotations, original warnings, and decision notes.

25
00:01:57,895 --> 00:02:00,165
Check the context before sharing.

26
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:06,640
The calendar preview explains excluded items and shows the actual calendar file.

27
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,830
Downloading it does not add events automatically.

28
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,620
Unclear dates stay outside the calendar.

29
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:19,855
Built with Codex and the Devpost Learn Skill Pack, the finished app uses local English text rules.

30
00:02:19,855 --> 00:02:24,935
The downloadable version works offline, without a runtime model or A P I credits.

31
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,535
Try the public offline app on GitHub.

32
00:02:29,535 --> 00:02:34,625
This edited sequence uses actual browser screenshots and computer narration.

33
00:02:34,625 --> 00:02:37,055
Human review remains essential.
